{
 "$comment": "Row shape: {id, screen, sidecar?: true (run.mjs builds pcg_import into the app's target directory first), setup?: [rowIds], steps: [{op, target?, index? (the nth control of that name, on click and select; a negative index counts from the last), by?: 'label' (click and select: match `target` against the control's aria-label, else the text of the <label> around it, else the aria-label of its role=group -- uiProbe.ts's labelOf; rows of identical 'Move to'/'Drop' buttons and bare checkboxes are told apart this way), text? (a `type` text's {XDG_DATA_HOME} becomes this run's isolated XDG_DATA_HOME, so a typed folder lives and dies with the run), key?, ticks?, ms?}], marker, expect: [string], headingExact?: string (one h1-h3 must read exactly this, from the probe's headings), noHeadingMarkers?: true (no h1-h3 may carry ::before text, from the probe's headingMarkers), forbid?: [string], allowGlobalForbid?: [string], selectsNonEmpty?: [selectName], manual?: reason, notes}. `setup` is FLAT, not recursive: it runs only the listed rows' own `steps`, never THEIR `setup` -- a row meant to be reused as another row's setup entry must list every ancestor it itself needs, explicitly, in order (see e.g. `settings-theme-select-and-manage-themes-modal`'s own setup). `op: 'nativeFile'` (text: a path from the repo root) types that path into the native file dialog the previous step opened, OS-level input because the command channel only reaches the webview. `op: 'select'` (target, text) picks an `<option>` on the `<select>` located by `target` -- added to run.mjs because CreateCharacterForm's race/class selects carry no accessible name of their own (a `<select>`'s `nameOf()` is its full concatenated option text, since that's non-empty textContent, so `target` must be a substring unique to the wanted select's own option list, e.g. one of its option's exact text, not the select's id); `text` is matched against each `<option>`'s own text/value. `op: 'scroll'` takes an optional `direction: 'up'|'down'` (default 'down', unchanged from before) -- 'up' exists because resetToLanding() (run before every row's own setup/steps) clicks RESET_CLICK_NAMES by raw xdotool coordinate, not the DOM channel, and cannot recover a target scrolled to a negative on-screen y (a tall form's own 'Back'/'Cancel' pushed off the top by content added below it, e.g. a create-character outcome panel) -- a row that leaves the page scrolled down should scroll back up as its own last step so the NEXT row's resetToLanding can find a landing-reachable control; see create-character-fill-and-submit's own trailing scroll step. Generated docs/testing/ui-smoke-inventory.md is rendered FROM this file by render-inventory.mjs -- edit this file, not the doc. Names in `target`/`selectsNonEmpty` are matched against the live uiProbe.ts snapshot's targets/selects by exact `name` (trimmed textContent || aria-label || placeholder || title || id, and select#<n> for the handful of anonymous <select>s -- see uiProbe.ts). `expect`/`marker`/`forbid` strings are matched against bodyText, which is captured via `innerText` (respects CSS, e.g. `text-transform: uppercase` renders the text differently than its mixed-case source prop/string) -- assert the case that actually renders, not the source string. Global forbid strings (applied by run.mjs to every row unless listed in that row's own `allowGlobalForbid`): 'could be read from the corpus', 'failure', 'Failed to load', 'requires the desktop runtime', 'undefined', 'NaN', '[object Object]', and 'Loading' still present after the row's wait budget. Denominator discipline: run.mjs writes results.json with EVERY selected row present (status 'not-run', reason 'not executed') before any row executes, and each row's own entry is replaced in place as it finishes -- a run killed mid-way (e.g. a 10-minute shell-call timeout) leaves a results.json whose row count still matches the run's own denominator, with the unexecuted rows explicit as 'not-run', never silently absent (see lib/resultsSkeleton.mjs). `--resume` (with `--out` pointed at a directory that already holds a results.json from a prior invocation): skips re-running any row whose entry there is already 'green' or 'manual' (carried forward verbatim), and re-runs every other row ('not-run', 'red', 'blocked', or missing from that file entirely) -- see lib/resultsSkeleton.mjs's buildResumeState. The final summary line reads '<green>/<total> green, <red> red, <blocked> blocked, <manual> manual, <not-run> not-run (M = <total> rows)'; run.mjs exits non-zero if red, blocked, OR not-run is nonzero. Auto-recover: if 2 consecutive rows both look like a command-channel stall (resetToLanding never reaching a recognizable screen, or a click/type/key/select's own long retry budget -- CLICK_TARGET_WAIT_MS -- still running out; NOT a row that ran cleanly but asserted false), run.mjs relaunches the app once (driver.sh launch) and retries the CURRENT (second) row before recording it, capped at 3 relaunches per run; a retry that then passes gets 'auto-relaunch' as its own `reason`.",
